      "status": "under_investigation",
      "status_notes": "GO-2026-4559 (CVE-2026-27141): golang.org/x/net/http2 0.50.0 panics when it reads an HTTP/2 frame of type 0x0a to 0x0f, because of a missing nil check on the frame parser (https://go.dev/issue/77652, https://go.dev/cl/746180). It was introduced in x/net 0.50.0 and fixed in 0.51.0. The trivy-fips packages for Alpine 3.23 are published in the DHI security repository, which requires authentication, and their Go build information has not been read build by build for this advisory. Pending: reading /usr/bin/trivy in each published build of this package to find the first build that embeds golang.org/x/net 0.51.0 or newer. The non-FIPS trivy package of the same releases embeds it from 0.69.2-r0 on."
    },
