      "status_notes": "GO-2026-4559 (CVE-2026-27141): golang.org/x/net/http2 0.50.0 panics when it reads an HTTP/2 frame of type 0x0a to 0x0f, because of a missing nil check on the frame parser (https://go.dev/issue/77652, https://go.dev/cl/746180). It was introduced in x/net 0.50.0 and fixed in 0.51.0. Each package installs one file, /usr/bin/trivy, a statically linked Go program for Linux (CGO_ENABLED=0 in every build). We read the Go build information (go version -m) and the function table (go tool nm) of /usr/bin/trivy in all 38 trivy builds published for Alpine 3.23 as of 2026-11-27 (0.69.1-r0 to 0.74.0-r12), on both x86_64 and aarch64. Every build links the http2 frame reader ((*Framer).ReadFrame). 0.69.1-r0, the first published build, embeds golang.org/x/net 0.50.0 and is affected. 0.69.2-r0 is the first build with x/net 0.51.0, and every later build embeds 0.51.0 or newer, up to 0.63.0 in 0.74.0-r12."
    },
